    <string name="rule_R1">Remove dead, diseased and damaged wood first: cut back to healthy green wood.</string>
    <string name="rule_R2">Remove crossing canes (one of each pair) and canes growing into the centre: keep an open cup.</string>
    <string name="rule_R3">Cut no more than 5 mm above an outward bud, sloping away from it (the app snaps the cut).</string>
    <string name="rule_R4">Strong canes (over 10 mm) keep 4–6 buds, weak canes (7–10 mm) keep 2–4.</string>
    <string name="rule_R5">Canes thinner than a pencil (under 7 mm) go at the base.</string>
    <string name="rule_A1">Remove dead, diseased (canker) and damaged wood first, and suckers from the rootstock.</string>
    <string name="rule_A2">Remove strong branches growing into the centre and crossing branches: keep the centre open.</string>
    <string name="rule_A3">Watershoots (upright, vigorous, no flower buds) go at their base.</string>
    <string name="rule_A4">Shorten each leader by about a third, to an outward bud.</string>
    <string name="rule_A5">Remove no more than 20% of the crown in one winter; keep short twigs and spurs for fruit.</string>
